  "id": "impairment-index",
  "term": "impairment index",
  "definition": "In this source, an impairment index is a combined score based on observed reduction in reflex responses, sometimes alongside injury ratings, used to represent an animal’s overall condition or vitality after stress. It summarizes how impaired normal responses are, with higher impairment linked to a greater risk of delayed death in the study context.",
